{
  "answer": "**答案:awasca(也拼作 awasqa)。** 这是一种粗织的日常布料,印加高地的平民穿它做衣服,也用于军队。沿海地区则多穿较轻的棉质衣物。\n\n与它相对的是 **cumbi(qompi)**。这种细密的挂毯式织物用羊驼、小羊驼和骆马(vicuña)的纤维织成,只供皇帝、贵族和宗教场合使用,由国家作坊里的专业织工制作。\n\n各来源在细节上略有出入。有的说 awasca 是用于毯子和地毯的粗羊驼毛或美洲驼毛织物,有的则把毯子归为更粗的 chusi。我只搜了一次,没有核实线密度之类的具体数据。\n\nSources:\n- [Inca Textiles – World History Encyclopedia](https://www.worldhistory.org/article/791/inca-textiles/.md)\n- [Textile arts of the Indigenous peoples of the Americas – Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Textile_arts_of_the_Indigenous_peoples_of_the_Americas)\n- [Inca Cumbi: Precolumbian Tapestry Traditions](https://scalar.usc.edu/works/andean-tapestry/inca-cumbi)\n- [Andean textiles – Textiles Cusco](https://www.textilescusco.org/andean-textiles)",
